> Not sure what you mean by this... if the offending BlendSpace is the currently open node, the error is visible as the current error on the persistent label, same as in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117275. It is also visible in the log.

Even if it is not currently open, it means that errors within a nest should always be displayed while it is blended. This is because the actual scene is currently experiencing issues on the viewport. Conversely, if the Blend amount is 0 or if it is a BlendSpace that is not connected, there is no need to always display it, so a warning is sufficient.


Currently, I am not sure if `AnimationNode::make_invalid()` is being utilized effectively, but for example, in the following BlendSpace2D code, when the line returning `return NodeTimeInfo();` is executed, it means that an error occurs in the actual viewport. Therefore, it should always be displayed as an error in the AnimationTreeEditorDock.

```cpp
